{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Observation\n\n`show_ticket` always computes `inbound_deps` by byte-scanning every event file in the store (src/rebar/reducer/_inbound.py, lines 39-72). On a clone of the live store, 2026-10-29, that is 139,978 files and 609 MB read per call. Only CREATE, EDIT, LINK, UNLINK and SNAPSHOT events change deps or parent (src/rebar/reducer/_replay.py). Restricting the scan to those types read 13,258 files and 150.5 MB, and found all 15 confirmed inbound links for the 1 ticket tested.\n\nCaveats:\n- The scan trusts that the filename suffix matches the event type inside the file.\n- Link targets are stored as written, so a link stored by alias is missed by an id byte scan. That gap exists in the current scan too; on the clone, 2 of 1,605 LINK targets are not canonical ids, and both are free text.\n\nRe-checked 2026-10-29 on a fresh copy at origin/main ca6810a4: one scan for d70a-97d9 opens 141,085 files and reads 609.5 MB. In `_replay.py`'s handler table, `parent_id` is set only by CREATE and by EDIT `fields`, `deps` only by LINK/UNLINK, and SNAPSHOT restores both; REVERT acts only on ARCHIVED. Event files are written as `{timestamp}-{uuid}-{EVENT_TYPE}.json`. `-PRECONDITIONS-SNAPSHOT.json` files also end in `-SNAPSHOT.json` but are not replayed, so the suffix test excludes them.\n\n## Plan\n1. Restrict the inbound scan to files ending in `-CREATE.json`, `-EDIT.json`, `-LINK.json`, `-UNLINK.json` or `-SNAPSHOT.json`, excluding `-PRECONDITIONS-SNAPSHOT.json`, before opening them. Update the module docstring and the docstring in src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/labels.py that describes the scan.\n2. Test first (seen failing on current code): a fixture with one inbound relationship in each of CREATE (parent), EDIT (re-parent), LINK, and a SNAPSHOT-compacted ticket, all found; a COMMENT naming the target that must not make its ticket a candidate; and an open() spy asserting no other event type is opened.\n3. Compare on a copy of the live store: for 50 sampled tickets plus the 15-link ticket, compute the old result by running `find_inbound_relationships` with the old all-files candidate scan (one shared pass over the store computing every sampled id's candidates, verbatim old matching) and the new result with the new scan; require equality, and record files and bytes read per call before and after.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [x] The scan opens only CREATE, EDIT, LINK, UNLINK and SNAPSHOT event files; verified by the open() spy test in tests/scripts/reducer/test_inbound_relationship_scan.py.\n- [x] inbound_deps is identical to the current code for at least 50 tickets sampled from a clone of the live store; recorded in a ticket comment with the sample size and files/bytes read per call before and after.\n\n## File impact (expected)\n- src/rebar/reducer/_inbound.py\n- src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/labels.py\n- tests/scripts/reducer/test_inbound_relationship_scan.py"}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793330770849951001,"uuid":"90e611ce-abb7-404c-ab6b-bb92eff69258"}